+No production generator change was made. The retained source-bound audit remains relevant: the occupancy-only rival agrees with all 96 sampled generated labels because the declared shared-picture grammar forbids rows whose aligned cells are both nonzero but differ in value. The canonical authority would retain such a value-differing row and emit an all-zero output row, as shown by the retained color-only branch counterexample. Expanding that semantic surface would require a deliberate generator/validator redesign rather than a small peer patch; it remains an explicit learnability/domain limitation.
